       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The label doesn't support it. The FDA-approved maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, so it is double the labeled maximum. Your reason was that the dose is within the label, so it doesn't apply here. If you have a label section that says otherwise, please check it again. The 1700 mg figure may be a total daily dose.\n\nThese are the orders I can enter right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **Another dose within the labeled range**\n\nIf you want a dose above the label maximum for a specific clinical reason, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. Tell me which dose to enter and I'll do it."
      }
